; SNOWFLAKE.LGO - the Koch snowflake, a famous fractal
;
; Every straight side is replaced by four shorter sides with a bump in
; the middle, and every one of those by four more, and so on. The
; LEVEL input says how many times to do the replacing.

to side :size :level
  if :level = 0 [forward :size stop]
  side :size / 3 :level - 1
  left 60
  side :size / 3 :level - 1
  right 120
  side :size / 3 :level - 1
  left 60
  side :size / 3 :level - 1
end

to snowflake :size :level
  repeat 3 [side :size :level right 120]
end

clearscreen
penup setxy -180 100 setheading 90 pendown
setpencolor [30 120 210]
snowflake 360 4
hideturtle
